{
	"schema": "formulas.rule-operators",
	"description": "Every comparison a person can put in a filter rule, as DATA. A rule names a field, one operator id from this file and its params; compile-rules.mjs turns it into a binding by filling the operator template, and evaluate-binding.mjs evaluates that binding. Adding a comparison is one row here, over the operators evaluate-binding.mjs runs. `applies_to` lists the field kinds (a field descriptor kind) that offer it, in menu order. `input` says what the person supplies: none, value (one), values (a list), words (a list of words), text, day or range (min and/or max). Template markers are objects: {\"$field\":\"path\"} is the field path, {\"$param\":\"name\"} is a param. `each` repeats `binding` once per entry of a list param (bound to `as`) and joins the copies with `combine`; `parts` keeps only the parts whose `when` param is present and joins them with `combine`. `negate` appends op:core.not. `param_case: lower` lower-cases text params, matching a template that lower-cases the field.",
